00:52:12,787 --> 00:52:17,209
We really, we tried, but we were stretched too thin.

640
00:52:17,229 --> 00:52:18,730
And then we had a couple of people who were,

641
00:52:20,028 --> 00:52:20,729
not going to be there.

642
00:52:20,749 --> 00:52:24,512
So you can only stretch so far.

643
00:52:24,532 --> 00:52:25,293
Absolutely.

644
00:52:25,673 --> 00:52:27,675
And I know you're doing everything you can.

645
00:52:27,915 --> 00:52:30,077
And I apologize to the community for this.

646
00:52:30,117 --> 00:52:32,319
My frustration is absolutely not with you all.

647
00:52:32,379 --> 00:52:37,324
It's never anything that we wanted to happen this summer, but yeah.

648
00:52:38,004 --> 00:52:39,345
Any further questions from the council?

649
00:52:39,365 --> 00:52:41,427
I know there's probably some members of the public would like to speak.

650
00:52:41,707 --> 00:52:43,329
Just to drive that point home again,

651
00:52:44,018 --> 00:52:46,240
We know that you're trying to make it work.

652
00:52:46,280 --> 00:53:02,872
We know that the people at the library, there are people at the library who have stayed years and decades longer, knowing they could get a job somewhere else, wanting to put in the effort, wanting to make this library everything it can be, wanting to put in that extra moment, knowing that if they left, there might not be someone else who would do the same.

653
00:53:03,372 --> 00:53:04,793
So we know it's not on you guys.

654
00:53:05,554 --> 00:53:07,335
We know 100% it's not on you guys.

655
00:53:07,455 --> 00:53:09,536
I just want, if it gets out to the community that,

656
00:53:10,437 --> 00:53:12,119
This is not anything we ever wanted.

657
00:53:12,279 --> 00:53:13,600
We're really very upset about it.

658
00:53:14,000 --> 00:53:20,266
And I think that was a really helpful question from Councilor Knight to understand why, you know, the most popular day, because there's a lot of layers.

659
00:53:20,506 --> 00:53:20,826
Yeah.

660
00:53:20,946 --> 00:53:21,667
And that's it.

661
00:53:22,348 --> 00:53:23,348
We appreciate your knowledge.

662
00:53:24,690 --> 00:53:30,955
Seeing no further questions from the Council at this time, are there any members who would like, any members of the public who would like to speak either on Zoom or in person?

663
00:53:30,975 --> 00:53:31,936
Thank you.

664
00:53:32,616 --> 00:53:33,137
Thank you, Barbara.

665
00:53:39,054 --> 00:53:40,075
Name and address for the record, please.

666
00:53:40,095 --> 00:53:46,060
Good evening, I'm Ellen Tonello, and my address is 177 Lincoln Road, Medford.

667
00:53:46,881 --> 00:53:50,764
And I am the chair trustee to the Medford Public Library.

668
00:53:51,805 --> 00:53:59,972
I have been with the library for a little bit better than 27 years in the role of a trustee.

669
00:54:01,013 --> 00:54:03,956
And I first wanna start by saying thank you

670
00:54:04,799 --> 00:54:16,983
to the former councilors and the former mayors and the current councilors that have been so supportive with the building and the budget of our library.

671
00:54:17,943 --> 00:54:23,064
There are a couple of things that I would like for you to be aware of this evening.

672
00:54:24,245 --> 00:54:27,886
One of them just happened this past Friday afternoon.

673
00:54:28,606 --> 00:54:32,227
I stopped into the library and there was a van

674
00:54:33,072 --> 00:54:46,902
from the fire department of Amherst, Massachusetts, that brought down eight members of the Amherst library, patrons, trustees, administration.

675
00:54:47,803 --> 00:55:00,012
They came because they were told that the city of Medford just built a library beyond, and they wanted to see what our library looked like.

676
00:55:00,672 --> 00:55:04,213
So they had a reference of what they could do in their city.

677
00:55:05,733 --> 00:55:12,455
Our building is now equivalent to the size of one full city block.

678
00:55:13,375 --> 00:55:29,359
It requires the attention of maintenance and the town and the city's government here to see to it that the building that over a thousand people donated money to

679
00:55:30,358 --> 00:55:47,151
or a three-year-old painted a tile to be placed on the wall in the children's department, that this building that they sought to, that they gave to, remains the building that it is.

680
00:55:48,472 --> 00:56:00,141
And I ask you, and I know you're working extremely hard with the budget, that you see to it that our facility is taken care of, that the budget

681
00:56:00,572 --> 00:56:08,594
which we're discussing this evening, not only are we understaffed, but we need to be sure that this building remains.

682
00:56:08,974 --> 00:56:14,975
While I was sitting here, I just happened to look up and I noticed these are fluorescent light bulbs.

683
00:56:15,615 --> 00:56:19,296
There is not a light bulb in the library to change.

684
00:56:20,376 --> 00:56:28,218
We are so modern in our technology that we need to secure someone that will see to it

685
00:56:28,652 --> 00:56:38,097
that this building stays the way it was built, and it represents all of us from young to old, and that it's cared for.

686
00:56:38,838 --> 00:56:44,961
So I just ask that you please give full attention to maintenance.

687
00:56:45,061 --> 00:56:49,203
It's not a janitor that cleans the building daily.

688
00:56:49,884 --> 00:56:55,927
It's the management that we should have to protect this building.

689
00:56:56,812 --> 00:57:16,881
And I will close just by saying we had a dedication a week ago, and we had a gentleman who had a humble beginning here in Medford and came to celebrate that had donated $3 million.

690
00:57:18,181 --> 00:57:26,225
$3 million is a wonderful gift, but the painting of a three-year-old on a tile is just as important

691
00:57:26,745 --> 00:57:28,246
as that large donation.

692
00:57:30,508 --> 00:57:39,416
We, I may stand to be corrected, but at our last meeting, our treasurer is not here with us this evening.

693
00:57:40,356 --> 00:57:54,368
But a fact that you may not know is the households in the city pay only $5 a month for that building.

694
00:57:55,640 --> 00:58:07,468
And that's very, very short money when you see the building that it houses for your children, for your seniors, for your teenagers.

695
00:58:08,428 --> 00:58:21,317
So I ask that you do put pressure on our government to increase our budget and see to it that the work that Barbara Kerr has put in and her staff are rewarded.

696
00:58:21,337 --> 00:58:23,078
So I thank you very much.

697
00:58:24,077 --> 00:58:24,597
Thank you, Helen.

698
00:58:24,637 --> 00:58:29,758
Thank you for your many years of service.

699
00:58:29,818 --> 00:58:33,079
Tom Lincoln 27 Gleason Street in sunny Medford.

700
00:58:33,799 --> 00:58:45,802
