721
01:00:18,137 --> 01:00:22,037
But since you are advocates, I am asking that you advocate for city employees.

722
01:00:22,718 --> 01:00:27,079
The city has not settled contracts for most of the city employees.

723
01:00:27,799 --> 01:00:33,480
That's the teachers, the carpenters, the secretaries, the paraprofessionals, and the librarians.

724
01:00:34,389 --> 01:00:45,814
The inability to find equitable terms for salary means that most of our city employees are taking pay cuts right now because of the cost of inflation, the cost of fuel to get to our jobs from our jobs.

725
01:00:47,415 --> 01:00:52,917
So I'm asking the city to find a plan to ensure that city employees get their compensation.

726
01:00:54,366 --> 01:01:09,892
so that we can retain our employees and so that when job openings occur, we can get qualified applicants so that we can keep all of our buildings and all of our different services up to the level that they've always been.

727
01:01:10,652 --> 01:01:13,193
So please help us.

728
01:01:14,053 --> 01:01:14,433
Thank you.

729
01:01:14,893 --> 01:01:15,093
Thanks.

730
01:01:15,214 --> 01:01:19,435
