01:05:30,607 --> 01:05:39,991
I know we have a lot to get through tonight, but I think this is just such an important point that I really wanted to underline it to, you know, reaffirm what we heard from people in the audience, Councilor Sang, Vice President Behrs.

784
01:05:40,952 --> 01:05:45,914
You know, it's been said many times by many, many people, a budget is a statement of values.

785
01:05:46,634 --> 01:05:54,718
And I think it's worth saying and worth acknowledging that putting together a budget under a budget crunch after two years of a pandemic, two and a half years, is not easy.

786
01:05:54,758 --> 01:05:56,539
It's not easy for the people in positions of power.

787
01:05:56,599 --> 01:05:58,440
It's not easy for the decision makers.

788
01:05:59,435 --> 01:06:04,776
But this is the role that we chose, the people it's really hard for.

789
01:06:04,796 --> 01:06:19,019
The people that this really comes down on are the people who are forced to do more with less, the people who are forced to effectively take pay cuts when you factor in inflation, the people who seek out city services, expecting city services and don't get what they need.

790
01:06:19,039 --> 01:06:21,860
This is what it comes down to.

791
01:06:22,680 --> 01:06:27,721
