So a vendor called and asked if I knew anything about Method's rink being open.

1342
01:54:10,139 --> 01:54:15,581
Then I found out that we might be opening the rink during the hottest months of the season this year for the first time ever.

1343
01:54:15,601 --> 01:54:16,982
Is that true?

1344
01:54:18,152 --> 01:54:18,813
That is correct.

1345
01:54:18,973 --> 01:54:22,538
Our goal is to try to open it up after July 4th, so July 5th.

1346
01:54:23,539 --> 01:54:31,190
It does depend on getting the ice built, but our goal is to open up July 5th or somewhere around that time.

1347
01:54:32,005 --> 01:54:36,888
have we done a cost analysis of how much it's going to cost to keep that rink open?

1348
01:54:37,328 --> 01:54:38,549
Because I know what it's going to cost.

1349
01:54:38,649 --> 01:54:39,569
It's a lot of money.

1350
01:54:40,170 --> 01:54:45,933
To keep that pump going during the hot months, it's a lot of money.

1351
01:54:46,634 --> 01:54:51,877
And so I would like to see, before we vote on this budget, Kevin, that

1352
01:54:52,677 --> 01:55:05,707
If we did a cost analysis to see if we have vendors that are coming in that are going to pay the fee because we were an established rank and we couldn't even come close to making sure that we can make that rank run with the money.

1353
01:55:06,207 --> 01:55:13,632
So I would also like to see what method programs are going to be running that rank during those months because

1354
01:55:14,573 --> 01:55:22,398
I just don't in this fiscal crisis that we're in right now to see that we're going to open up the rank during the hottest months without knowing.

1355
01:55:23,627 --> 01:55:28,672
The impacts, whether pro or con, I think it's going to be tough to swallow.

1356
01:55:31,234 --> 01:55:32,515
Hard numbers are hard numbers.

1357
01:55:32,555 --> 01:55:40,983
And I'm sure the electric company can give you the estimated cost of what that rink's going to be charged per month to run for their compressor.

1358
01:55:41,103 --> 01:55:42,244
I know it's a lot of money.

1359
01:55:42,304 --> 01:55:44,706
So I mean, that's going to be another issue.

1360
01:55:44,726 --> 01:55:47,548
And then my last question, so everybody else can speak.

1361
01:55:47,568 --> 01:55:48,729
I know people have other questions.

1362
01:55:50,430 --> 01:55:54,611
that making sure that there's a good relationship with Chevalier.

1363
01:55:54,651 --> 01:55:59,532
I know as we move forward, that that space is vital right now.

1364
01:55:59,712 --> 01:56:07,453
We were hoping, you know, in past months, talking about different facilities in the city to make them our new recreational facility.

1365
